          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"cofield-nikkis-touch-c148b6e111b58278\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Nikki’s responsive “I love you too, Franco” primarily avows her loving emotional state. Its reciprocal placement mildly ratifies their relationship, but it does not clearly undertake a promise or obligation. Her emotion-laden delivery does not independently establish expressive/reflexive force: the utterance remains adequately represented as an emotional but deliberate avowal.\",\"ambiguity\":\"There is slight uncertainty over whether the reciprocal declaration carries enough relational ratification to count as weak performative force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Nikki directly addresses Franco in response to his declaration of love.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Franco has just offered a considered and explicitly sincere declaration, and Nikki reciprocates after reflecting that she has found the secure love she had wanted. Her subsequent statement that she is glad she found him and the narration of her deep care support sincerity. The wedding setting and mutual recognition add relational significance, but neither they nor her voice being “thick with emotion” turn the words into a clear commitment or reflex-like discharge.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I love you too, Franco,” she said.\",\"supports\":\"The first-person reciprocal declaration strongly supports truth-conditional avowal and identifies a direct utterance to Franco.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Franco first says, “I love you, Nikki,” explains that he did not want to rush, and says he now knows the love is real.\",\"supports\":\"Nikki’s “too” is an intelligible reciprocal response to a considered declaration, with weak relational-ratification pressure toward P.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Nikki’s “voice [is] thick with emotion,” and she adds, “I’m so glad I found you.”\",\"supports\":\"The delivery is emotionally intense and the declaration is presented as sincere, but there is no positive evidence that the words themselves are a reflex-like discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.95},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration says Nikki realizes she has already found the love she once dreamed of and later describes Franco as someone she has come to care for deeply.\",\"supports\":\"The surrounding narration independently corroborates the loving state avowed by the utterance.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is marked as an affirmative present-tense explicit I-love-you construction and retained as VALID_EXPLICIT_LOVE_I_YOU.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms that the highlighted wording is an ordinary affirmative love declaration rather than a negated or merely metalinguistic occurrence.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T captures the central avowal, while a low P score records limited reciprocal relational ratification. Emotional delivery is contextual evidence rather than independent E force, and no residual core function requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
